  "site_map": "# Five 124-byte status predicate entries\n\nFull retail range 0xE2BB0..0xE2E1C (620 bytes), runtime 0x800C8310..0x800C857C, was read end to end in retail.asm. Each body is 31 instructions, leaf/no frame/no allocated data. Predicate masks in retail order: 0x00080000, 0x08000000, 0x02000000, 0x10000000, 0x00100000. The bodies differ only in those two LUI immediates per predicate.\n\nEntry evidence: first predicate is JAL-called by four registered DUNGEON bank rows, independently verified in the actual container (evidence/status_helpers_entries.json). The other four predicates have actual registered engine JAL callers from the existing primary call census. The physical row id for the first is dungeon/func_800C2BB0 and its true runtime function is func_800C8310; do not confuse it with the existing nominal func_800C8310 row, whose true function is elsewhere.\n\nRoles: a0 begins as entity pointer; flags14 bit0x4000 selects aggregate behavior. Direct branch loads signed/word entity+0x54 into v1 and tests the mask, returning 1 or0. Aggregate branch loads the resident EntityRec pointer at D_800E3D7C. a0 becomes descending index1..0; v1 starts at root+4, and links are loaded at cursor+0xAC, then cursor-=4, selecting root's pointer fields +0xB0 then+0xAC. v0 is the linked object pointer, then its +0x54 flags. a1 holds the mask. Null links skip. A set bit branches to common return with li v0,1 in the branch delay. Loop exhaustion jumps to common return with v0=0 in the jump delay. Direct branch is after the loop, then common jr ra/nop. No GP accesses, stores or calls occur inside the predicates.\n\nAttribution: load-only, family-neutral predicates give no conflicting store-emission signature. Use the surrounding uniform proven engine/cohort GCC2.7.2-cdk -O2 -G0 recipe and the unchanged lineage scanner; no compiler sweep ranking is used. Plain pointer/loop C owns the initial reconstruction. All source/ABI statements follow actual registered callers and the shared EntityRec pointer fields; no accounting stub is inferred.\n",
